<w:document xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:wp="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><w:body><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Cambria" w:hAnsi="Cambria" w:cs="Cambria"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">1. Paper and the printed page</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="both"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">A document meets its reader on a sheet of paper or on a screen that pretends to be one. The size of that sheet decides where every line ends, where every page breaks and how much of a table fits across. A converter that reads the size wrong moves every word that follows, so the paper is the first thing a faithful conversion must get right.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="both"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">Two families of sizes share the world. The ISO 216 series starts from a sheet of one square metre whose sides keep the ratio of one to the square root of two, so that halving a sheet gives the next size with the same shape. North America keeps the inch sizes of its paper mills: Letter, Legal, Tabloid and Executive, whose shapes owe nothing to one another.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="both"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">Orientation turns a sheet on its side. A portrait page is taller than it is wide; a landscape page is the same sheet turned a quarter, which suits a wide table, a chart with many columns or a slide. The sheet does not change, only the direction the text runs across it.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Cambria" w:hAnsi="Cambria" w:cs="Cambria"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">1.1 How a section states its paper</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="both"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">A word processor stores the page size with each section of the document, together with its margins, its header and its footer. When a section ends, the next one may change the size, turn the page or both, so a single file can mix a portrait report with a landscape appendix printed on a larger sheet.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:ind w:left="720" w:right="720"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Times New Roman" w:hAnsi="Times New Roman" w:cs="Times New Roman"/><w:i/><w:sz w:val="24"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">The page is the unit of reading. A reader remembers that a passage sat at the top of a left-hand page long after the words themselves have faded, and a converter that moves the break moves that memory with it.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="both"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">A spreadsheet states its paper per sheet, by a numbered code from a table of paper sizes, with an orientation and a scale. A presentation states one slide size for the whole deck, and each slide is drawn on a page of exactly that size.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline distT="0" distB="0" distL="0" distR="0"><wp:extent cx="2743200" cy="1371600"/><wp:effectExtent l="0" t="0" r="0" b="0"/><wp:docPr id="1" name="Picture 1" descr="Three coloured shapes in a frame"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="1" name="picture.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId10"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="2743200" cy="1371600"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Caption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">A picture placed inline with the text keeps its size on every paper.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Cambria" w:hAnsi="Cambria" w:cs="Cambria"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">2. Measures that follow the width</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="both"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">The measure is the length of a line of text. On a narrow sheet such as A5 the measure shrinks and a paragraph takes more lines; on a wide sheet such as A3 in landscape the measure grows and the same paragraph takes fewer. Every page break after the first moves accordingly, which is why a document must be laid out again, not scaled, when the paper changes.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:jc w:val="both"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t xml:space="preserve">Headings keep with the paragraph that follows them, so a heading never sits alone at the foot of a page. Tables split between rows, and a row that fits on no page is cut where the page ends. Pictures stay with the line that holds them and push that line to the next page when they do not fit.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:tbl><w:tblPr><w:tblStyle w:val="TableGrid"/><w:tblW w:w="5000" w:type="pct"/><w:tblLook w:val="04A0" w:firstRow="1" w:lastRow="0" w:firstColumn="1" w:lastColumn="0" w:noHBand="0" w:noVBand="1"/></w:tblPr><w:tblGrid><w:gridCol w:w="2340"/><w:gridCol w:w="2340"/><w:gridCol w:w="2340"/><w:gridCol w:w="2340"/></w:tblGrid><w:tr><w:trPr><w:tblHeader/></w:trPr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/><w:shd w:val="clear" w:color="auto" w:fill="D9E1F2"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial" w:cs="Arial"/><w:b/><w:sz w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">Paper</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/><w:shd w:val="clear" w:color="auto" w:fill="D9E1F2"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial" w:cs="Arial"/><w:b/><w:sz w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">Series</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/><w:shd w:val="clear" w:color="auto" w:fill="D9E1F2"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial" w:cs="Arial"/><w:b/><w:sz w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">Width</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/><w:shd w:val="clear" w:color="auto" w:fill="D9E1F2"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial" w:cs="Arial"/><w:b/><w:sz w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">Height</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc></w:tr><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial" w:cs="Arial"/><w:sz w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">A3</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial" w:cs="Arial"/><w:sz w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">ISO 216</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial" w:cs="Arial"/><w:sz w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">297 mm</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial" w:cs="Arial"/><w:sz w:val="20"/></w:rPr><w:t xml:space="preserve">420 mm</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:tc></w:tr><w:tr><w:tc><w:tcPr><w:tcW w:w="1250" w:type="pct"/></w:tcPr><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="0"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rFonts w:ascii="Arial" w:hAnsi="Arial"